import json

notebook = {
    "cells": [
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "# Real-World Data (RWD) Medallion Pipeline for Diabetic Patient Readmission Risk\n",
                "\n",
                "## 1. High-Level Project Overview\n",
                "This notebook implements an end-to-end **Databricks Medallion Architecture** using PySpark to process raw, semi-structured Electronic Health Records (EHR) into standardized biopharmaceutical industry metrics[cite: 2].\n",
                "\n",
                "```text\n",
                " 🥉 BRONZE LAYER (`bronze_ehr_raw`)\n",
                " └── Ingests and stores raw JSON EHR strings along with ingestion metadata.\n",
                "       │\n",
                "       ▼\n",
                " 🥈 SILVER LAYER (`silver_patient_omop`)\n",
                " └── Parses JSON, cleans data, deduplicates records, and maps ICD-10 diagnosis codes to OMOP CDM concept IDs.\n",
                "       │\n",
                "       ▼\n",
                " 🥇 GOLD LAYER (`gold_diabetic_metrics`)\n",
                " └── Calculates pre-aggregated business metrics (patient counts, readmission counts, and 30-day readmission percentages).\n",
                "```"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### Step 1: Ingestion & Creation of the Bronze Layer\n",
                "\n",
                "#### Line-by-Line Code Breakdown:\n",
                "* **`from pyspark.sql import SparkSession`**: Imports the primary entry point for PySpark DataFrame and SQL functionality[cite: 2].\n",
                "* **`from pyspark.sql.functions import ...`**: Imports PySpark SQL functions used for column selection, JSON parsing, timestamp casting, expressions, and conditional logic[cite: 2].\n",
                "* **`from pyspark.sql.types import ...`**: Imports PySpark data types required to explicitly construct structural schemas for complex, nested JSON payloads[cite: 2].\n",
                "* **`raw_data = [...]`**: Defines a list of tuples containing raw JSON strings (simulating landing EHR records) and their corresponding ingestion timestamps[cite: 2].\n",
                "* **`bronze_df = spark.createDataFrame(...)`**: Converts the Python in-memory list into a distributed PySpark DataFrame with named columns[cite: 2].\n",
                "* **`bronze_df.write.format(\"delta\").mode(\"overwrite\").saveAsTable(\"bronze_ehr_raw\")`**: Saves the DataFrame as an immutable, managed Delta table named `bronze_ehr_raw` in overwrite mode[cite: 2].\n",
                "* **`print(\"Bronze Table Created!\")`**: Outputs a status message confirming execution completion[cite: 2]."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": None,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "from pyspark.sql import SparkSession\n",
                "from pyspark.sql.functions import col, from_json, to_timestamp, current_timestamp, expr, when\n",
                "from pyspark.sql.types import StructType, StructField, StringType, IntegerType, ArrayType\n",
                "\n",
                "# 1. Create Mock Raw JSON EHR Data (Bronze Layer)\n",
                "raw_data = [\n",
                "    ('{\"patient_id\": \"P-101\", \"gender\": \"F\", \"dob\": \"1968-05-14\", \"diagnoses\": [{\"code\": \"E11.9\", \"desc\": \"Type 2 Diabetes\"}], \"readmitted_30d\": 1}', \"2026-09-20 08:00:00\"),\n",
                "    ('{\"patient_id\": \"P-102\", \"gender\": \"M\", \"dob\": \"1975-11-22\", \"diagnoses\": [{\"code\": \"I10\", \"desc\": \"Hypertension\"}], \"readmitted_30d\": 0}', \"2026-09-20 08:05:00\"),\n",
                "    ('{\"patient_id\": \"P-103\", \"gender\": \"F\", \"dob\": \"1954-01-30\", \"diagnoses\": [{\"code\": \"E11.65\", \"desc\": \"Type 2 Diabetes with Hyperglycemia\"}], \"readmitted_30d\": 1}', \"2026-09-20 08:10:00\"),\n",
                "    ('{\"patient_id\": \"P-104\", \"gender\": \"M\", \"dob\": \"1982-08-03\", \"diagnoses\": [{\"code\": \"E11.9\", \"desc\": \"Type 2 Diabetes\"}], \"readmitted_30d\": 0}', \"2026-09-20 08:15:00\")\n",
                "]\n",
                "\n",
                "bronze_df = spark.createDataFrame(raw_data, [\"raw_json_payload\", \"ingestion_time\"])\n",
                "# Write as Bronze Delta Table\n",
                "bronze_df.write.format(\"delta\").mode(\"overwrite\").saveAsTable(\"bronze_ehr_raw\")\n",
                "print(\"Bronze Table Created!\")"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### Step 2: Data Cleaning & OMOP CDM Standardization (Silver Layer)\n",
                "\n",
                "#### Line-by-Line Code Breakdown:\n",
                "* **`ehr_schema = StructType([...])`**: Defines an explicit schema for reading nested JSON attributes without incurring runtime schema-inference overhead[cite: 2].\n",
                "* **`spark.table(\"bronze_ehr_raw\")`**: Reads the raw data from the Bronze Delta storage table[cite: 2].\n",
                "* **`.withColumn(\"parsed\", from_json(col(\"raw_json_payload\"), ehr_schema))`**: Uses `from_json` to parse the JSON string column into a structured object[cite: 2].\n",
                "* **`.select(...)`**: Unpacks struct elements into discrete relational columns[cite: 2]:\n",
                "  * `col(\"parsed.patient_id\").alias(\"person_source_value\")`: Maps patient identifier to OMOP CDM naming conventions[cite: 2].\n",
                "  * `col(\"parsed.gender\").alias(\"gender_source_value\")`: Extracts gender values[cite: 2].\n",
                "  * `to_timestamp(col(\"parsed.dob\"), \"yyyy-MM-dd\").alias(\"birth_datetime\")`: Converts string date into a Spark timestamp[cite: 2].\n",
                "  * `expr(\"parsed.diagnoses[0].code\").alias(\"icd10_code\")`: Extracts the primary diagnosis code from the JSON array[cite: 2].\n",
                "  * `col(\"parsed.readmitted_30d\").alias(\"is_30day_readmitted\")`: Extracts the readmission indicator[cite: 2].\n",
                "  * `col(\"ingestion_time\")`: Retains record lineage metadata[cite: 2].\n",
                "* **`.withColumn(\"omop_concept_id\", when(...))`**: Conditional logic mapping hospital ICD-10 codes to standardized OMOP Concept IDs (`201826` for Type 2 Diabetes, `320128` for Essential Hypertension)[cite: 2].\n",
                "* **`.filter(col(\"person_source_value\").isNotNull())`**: Data validation step ensuring null patient keys are excluded[cite: 2].\n",
                "* **`.dropDuplicates([\"person_source_value\"])`**: Ensures individual patient uniqueness across the Silver layer[cite: 2].\n",
                "* **`silver_df.write.format(\"delta\").mode(\"overwrite\").saveAsTable(\"silver_patient_omop\")`**: Saves processed records to the `silver_patient_omop` Delta table[cite: 2]."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": None,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# 2. Define Schema for JSON Parsing\n",
                "ehr_schema = StructType([\n",
                "    StructField(\"patient_id\", StringType(), True),\n",
                "    StructField(\"gender\", StringType(), True),\n",
                "    StructField(\"dob\", StringType(), True),\n",
                "    StructField(\"readmitted_30d\", IntegerType(), True),\n",
                "    StructField(\"diagnoses\", ArrayType(\n",
                "        StructType([\n",
                "            StructField(\"code\", StringType(), True),\n",
                "            StructField(\"desc\", StringType(), True)\n",
                "        ])\n",
                "    ), True)\n",
                "])\n",
                "\n",
                "# Process Bronze to Silver\n",
                "silver_df = (\n",
                "    spark.table(\"bronze_ehr_raw\")\n",
                "    .withColumn(\"parsed\", from_json(col(\"raw_json_payload\"), ehr_schema))\n",
                "    .select(\n",
                "        col(\"parsed.patient_id\").alias(\"person_source_value\"),\n",
                "        col(\"parsed.gender\").alias(\"gender_source_value\"),\n",
                "        to_timestamp(col(\"parsed.dob\"), \"yyyy-MM-dd\").alias(\"birth_datetime\"),\n",
                "        expr(\"parsed.diagnoses[0].code\").alias(\"icd10_code\"),\n",
                "        col(\"parsed.readmitted_30d\").alias(\"is_30day_readmitted\"),\n",
                "        col(\"ingestion_time\")\n",
                "    )\n",
                "    # Map ICD-10 to OMOP Concept ID (Standardization)\n",
                "    .withColumn(\"omop_concept_id\", \n",
                "        when(col(\"icd10_code\").startswith(\"E11\"), 201826) # OMOP Concept ID for Type 2 Diabetes\n",
                "        .otherwise(320128) # OMOP Concept ID for Essential Hypertension\n",
                "    )\n",
                "    .filter(col(\"person_source_value\").isNotNull())\n",
                "    .dropDuplicates([\"person_source_value\"])\n",
                ")\n",
                "\n",
                "silver_df.write.format(\"delta\").mode(\"overwrite\").saveAsTable(\"silver_patient_omop\")\n",
                "print(\"Silver Table Created!\")"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### Step 3: Clinical Endpoint Aggregations (Gold Layer)\n",
                "\n",
                "#### Line-by-Line Code Breakdown:\n",
                "* **`spark.table(\"silver_patient_omop\")`**: Reads cleaned and standardized records from the Silver layer[cite: 2].\n",
                "* **`.groupBy(\"omop_concept_id\")`**: Groups dataset rows by OMOP concept disease codes[cite: 2].\n",
                "* **`.agg(...)`**: Computes aggregated health metrics[cite: 2]:\n",
                "  * `expr(\"count(person_source_value)\").alias(\"total_patients\")`: Calculates total patient volume per diagnosis group[cite: 2].\n",
                "  * `expr(\"sum(is_30day_readmitted)\").alias(\"total_readmissions\")`: Sums total readmissions within a 30-day window[cite: 2].\n",
                "* **`.withColumn(\"readmission_rate_pct\", ...)`**: Derives percentage readmission metrics[cite: 2].\n",
                "* **`gold_df.write.format(\"delta\").mode(\"overwrite\").saveAsTable(...)`**: Persists aggregated business KPIs to the Gold layer[cite: 2].\n",
                "* **`display(gold_df)`**: Generates an interactive tabular display in Databricks[cite: 2]."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": None,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# 3. Gold Layer: Aggregated Clinical Metrics\n",
                "gold_df = (\n",
                "    spark.table(\"silver_patient_omop\")\n",
                "    .groupBy(\"omop_concept_id\")\n",
                "    .agg(\n",
                "        expr(\"count(person_source_value)\").alias(\"total_patients\"),\n",
                "        expr(\"sum(is_30day_readmitted)\").alias(\"total_readmissions\")\n",
                "    )\n",
                "    .withColumn(\"readmission_rate_pct\", (col(\"total_readmissions\") / col(\"total_patients\")) * 100)\n",
                ")\n",
                "\n",
                "gold_df.write.format(\"delta\").mode(\"overwrite\").saveAsTable(\"gold_diabetic_metrics\")\n",
                "display(gold_df)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### Step 4: Final Aggregated Results Table\n",
                "\n",
                "| omop_concept_id | total_patients | total_readmissions | readmission_rate_pct | Clinical Description |\n",
                "| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n",
                "| **201826** | 3 | 2 | 66.67% | Type 2 Diabetes[cite: 2] |\n",
                "| **320128** | 1 | 0 | 0.0% | Essential Hypertension[cite: 2] |"
            ]
        }
    ],
    "metadata": {
        "language_info": {
            "name": "python"
